UPDATE companies SET description='Apogee Semiconductor was founded in 2017 in Plano, Texas, launched with a National Science Foundation grant to solve the reliability problem of commercial off-the-shelf (COTS) components in space and defense applications. The founding team established the company as a U.S.-based supplier of radiation-hardened power, analog, and mixed-signal integrated circuits.

The company designs fault-containment ICs that serve as a protective architecture layer around COTS parts, rather than replacing every component. Its product portfolio includes radiation-hardened shift registers, I/O expanders, smart high-side power switches, level translators, majority voters, and GPIO expanders. Apogee operates a fabless model, partnering with qualified foundry, assembly, and test suppliers while maintaining oversight through documented processes and traceability. By 2022 the company had shipped 10,000 units, and its components achieved verified flight heritage in 2023.

Its components have been validated through NASA''s Tipping Point program and are used in mission-critical power architectures where deterministic fault containment and telemetry are required.

Apogee differentiates itself by building fault containment into the silicon architecture rather than screening commercial parts after fabrication. The company''s Zero-Power-Penalty™ cold-sparing technology eliminates leakage current in redundant circuits, and its LEO and GEO product variants share identical form, fit, and function to simplify design reuse. Apogee emphasizes engineer-to-engineer support, publishing all test data openly and responding to technical inquiries within 24 hours.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Radiation-hardened IC design", "Fault containment architecture", "Cold sparing (Zero-Power-Penalty)", "Level translation", "Smart high-side power switching", "Majority voting", "GPIO expansion", "Serial-in parallel-out shift registers", "JEDEC-qualified reliability testing (J-STD-020)", "Product change notification (J-STD-046)", "Design and change control", "Manufacturing and supplier oversight", "Reliability and qualification flows", "Continuous improvement processes"], "industries": ["Space", "Defense", "Aerospace", "Military", "Harsh environments"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fault containment built into silicon architecture, not screened after fabrication", "Zero-Power-Penalty\u2122 cold sparing eliminates leakage in redundant parts", "LEO and GEO variants share identical form, fit, and function", "Engineer-to-engineer support with 24-hour technical response and open test data", "Fabless model with qualified foundry/assembly/test partners and documented supplier oversight"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2017 in Plano, Texas with NSF grant -> /about-us", "Radiation-hardened power, analog, mixed-signal IC provider -> /about-us", "Fault containment architecture layer around COTS -> /about-us", "Zero-Power-Penalty cold sparing technology -> /about-us", "LEO and GEO variants share form, fit, function -> /about-us", "Engineer-to-engineer support, 24-hour response, open test data -> /about-us", "10,000 units shipped by 2022 -> /about-us", "Flight heritage established 2023 -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certified April 2024 -> /about-us", "NASA Tipping Point Award 2019 -> /about-us", "First product shipped August 2021 -> /about-us", "300 krad product family released 2023 -> /about-us", "Industry''s first GPIO expander May 2025 -> /about-us", "Industry''s smallest smart load switch family February 2026 -> /about-us", "Fabless model with qualified foundry, assembly, test partners -> /quality", "JEDEC J-STD-020 MSL characterization -> /quality", "JEDEC J-STD-046 product change notification -> /quality", "Product shelf life policies -> /quality", "CEO David Briggs, 34 years semiconductor experience -> /about-us", "Director Engineering Brett Smith, 25+ years experience -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Apogee is the only US-based high-reliability IC provider purpose-built for fault containment around COTS", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='apogee-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Apparatus Manufacturing began in 1986 on Commerce Street in Poughkeepsie, New York, when founder Norman Murley started with a welding booth and a tape-fed CNC machine. The family-owned, family-run shop remains at the same Hudson Valley address today, now led by Norman''s son Christopher.

The company specializes in precision sheet metal fabrication, offering cutting, forming, welding, assembly, and finishing for prototypes through production runs. Its facility runs autoloading fiber lasers, servo presses, and software-enabled process automation, and houses a fully automated powder coating line with ovens up to 118 by 59 by 31 inches, three color-change centers, a reclamation system, and four ITW Gema manual guns. Additional finishes include anodizing, silk screening, and engraving. Materials processed range from stainless steel, aluminum, and copper to mild steel and brass.

Apparatus serves commercial and retail markets, with documented work for IBM, Marriott, and UPS on products such as compact junction boxes and hotel kiosk enclosures. The customer base spans data centers, retail fixtures, medical equipment, scientific instruments, hospitality, restaurants, office furniture, logistics and warehousing, electrical enclosures, railway transport, and lighting.

The founder''s guiding principle—"Aim small, miss small"—reflects a commitment to parts that fit the first time at a competitive price. The company emphasizes value engineering from start to finish, leveraging automated finishing for speed and consistency while maintaining a hands-on, family-run culture.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision sheet metal fabrication", "Laser cutting (fiber laser)", "Forming (servo press)", "Welding", "Assembly", "Powder coating (automated with pretreatment)", "Anodizing", "Silk screening", "Engraving", "Value engineering", "Prototyping", "Production runs"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Retail", "Data center", "Electrical enclosures", "Retail fixtures", "Medical equipment", "Scientific", "Hospitality", "Restaurants", "Office furniture", "Logistics & warehousing", "Railway transport", "Lighting"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Mild steel", "Brass"], "equipment": ["Autoloading fiber lasers", "Servo presses", "Software-enabled process automation", "Powder coating ovens (118\" x 59\" x 31\")", "Three color-change powder centers", "Powder reclamation system", "Four ITW Gema manual powder coating guns", "Tape-fed CNC machine (historical)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1986 at the original Poughkeepsie location", "Fully automated powder coating facility with in-line pretreatment and dual stoving ovens", "Precision sheet metal fabrication from prototype to production with autoloading fiber lasers and servo presses", "Value engineering applied from design through delivery", "Trusted by major brands including IBM, Marriott, and UPS"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 in Poughkeepsie, NY by Norman Murley -> /about", "Family-owned, family-run, now led by Christopher Murley -> /about", "Precision sheet metal fabrication: cut, form, weld, assemble, finish -> /about", "Equipment: autoloading fiber lasers, servo presses, software-enabled process automation -> /about", "Automated powder coating facility with ovens up to 118x59x31 in, three color-change centers, reclamation, four ITW Gema guns -> /quality", "Additional finishes: anodizing, silk screening, engraving -> /quality", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, copper, mild steel, brass -> /about, /quality", "Industries served: commercial, retail, data center, retail fixtures, medical, scientific, hospitality, restaurants, office furniture, logistics, electrical enclosures, railway, lighting -> /, /quality", "Customers: IBM, Marriott, UPS -> /, /about", "Value engineering from start to finish -> /", "Aim small, miss small philosophy -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Apparatus Manufacturing delivers precision sheet metal fabrication solutions across industries of many kinds. At our local Hudson Valley facility, we service all custom metal fabrication needs, prototyping through production.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='apparatus-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Apparel Factory® operates from Los Angeles, California, supplying wholesale blank apparel to decorators and brands across the United States. The company does not disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founders in its public materials.

The catalog centers on decorator-ready basics: short- and long-sleeve tees, hoodies, crewnecks, quarter-zips, tank tops, and baseball jerseys sold under the AF Essential and Proline by AF® lines. Every style is marketed as print-ready, pre-shrunk, and equipped with tear-away labels to simplify relabeling. The company emphasizes eco-conscious production but does not publish facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures.

Customers include screen-print shops, direct-to-film (DTF) operators, merch programs, and streetwear labels. The homepage references "rush orders, tired printers" and positions the AF810 tee as a blank that "took the DTF like a pro" with "perfect adhesion, no cracking, no peeling." Hoodies such as the AF360 are described as doubling "as a perfect blank for merch drops and brand collections." Youth and women''s cuts extend the range for uniform and teamwear buyers.

Apparel Factory® highlights its eco-conscious production approach and decorator-focused features—pre-shrunk fabrics, tear-away labels, and printer-approved construction—as the core differentiators that attracted its customer base. Free shipping is offered on California orders over $350 and U.S. orders over $500 (excluding Alaska, Hawaii, and territories).', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale blank apparel distribution", "Custom apparel sourcing programs", "DTF-compatible blank selection", "Screen-print-compatible blank selection", "Eco-conscious production sourcing"], "industries": ["Apparel decoration", "Screen printing", "Direct-to-film (DTF) printing", "Merchandise branding", "Streetwear", "Promotional products", "Teamwear and uniforms"], "materials": ["CVC (cotton/polyester blend)", "Jersey knit", "Heavyweight cotton", "Performance polyester", "French terry fleece"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Company name and tagline -> db", "Headquarters: Los Angeles, California -> db", "Business description: Wholesale Blanks & Custom Apparel -> /", "Free shipping thresholds: $350 CA, $500 US -> /", "Product lines: AF Essential, Proline by AF -> /", "Specific SKUs and product details (AF810, AF360, etc.) -> /", "Fabric weights and compositions (4.7 oz to 14 oz) -> /", "Features: print-ready, pre-shrunk, tear-away label, printer-approved -> /", "Eco-conscious production mention -> db, /", "Customer references: printers, merch drops, brand collections -> /", "Youth and women''s cuts available -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Wholesale Blanks & Custom Apparel USA", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='apparel-factory-wholesale-premium-blank-custom-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Apparel MFG USA operates from a facility in Glendale, California, within Los Angeles County''s fashion corridor.

The shop delivers end-to-end garment manufacturing, covering product development (pattern making, grading, sampling, digitizing, fabric and trim sourcing), cut-and-sew production (cutting, sewing, finishing, pressing), private-label branding (screen printing, embroidery, heat transfers, labeling, packaging), and full-service packages that manage material procurement through logistics. All work is performed in-house at the Glendale plant, with capacity ranging from small runs of 50 units to larger orders of 5,000 units.

Clients include emerging designers, direct-to-consumer startups, celebrity labels, influencer-driven drops, and established retailers. The company produces a range of apparel categories such as t‑shirts, hoodies, activewear, loungewear, and outerwear, serving the fashion, streetwear, and retail sectors.

