UPDATE companies SET description='Axium Packaging’s California plant operates in Ontario, a facility opened in 2013 as part of a company founded in 2010 by the Judge Family Group. The business began with a bottle manufacturing launch in Mississauga, Ontario, Canada, and is led by CEO Pushminder Judge and President Paul Judge. Ownership remains with the Judge family, and the company holds minority-certified status.

The plant produces rigid plastic packaging using extrusion blow molding, injection stretch blow molding, injection blow molding, injection molding, and tube extrusion, supplemented by decoration and finishing services. Across the network, Axium runs 33 facilities totaling more than 4.7 million square feet of manufacturing space with a workforce exceeding 3,500. The integrated platform includes in-house design studios, 3D modeling, and tool shops that support concept-to-shelf development.

Customers span personal care and beauty, healthcare and nutraceuticals, food, beverage and spirits, and home and fabric care. The company serves multinational brands such as Unilever, Procter & Gamble, L’Oréal, Bath & Body Works, and Diageo, often through near-site manufacturing arrangements that shorten supply chains.

Axium differentiates itself with a speed-to-market model that cuts traditional lead times in half, a vertically integrated recycling subsidiary (Vertix) that supplies post-consumer recycled resin, and a unified quality system built on GFSI FSSC 22000 V6 standards across all sites.', certifications=ARRAY['GFSI FSSC 22000 V6','Minority-certified supplier']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion Blow Molding", "Injection Stretch Blow Molding", "Injection Blow Molding", "Injection Molding", "Tube Extrusion", "Decoration & Finishing", "Design & Engineering", "3D Modeling", "Tool Shop Services", "Vertix Recycling (PCR resin production)", "Quality Assurance (SPC, CMM, vision inspection)"], "industries": ["Personal Care & Beauty", "Healthcare & Nutraceuticals", "Food, Beverage & Spirits", "Home & Fabric Care"], "materials": ["Post-consumer recycled (PCR) resin", "Bioplastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Reduces development and shipping lead times from weeks to days", "Near-site manufacturing facilities boost capacity and cut carbon footprint", "Vertically integrated Vertix Recycling supplies PCR resin for sustainable packaging", "Unified quality system (GFSI FSSC 22000 V6) across all 33 facilities", "In-house design, tooling, and 3D modeling accelerate iteration cycles"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010, owned by Judge Family Group -> /about", "CEO Pushminder Judge, President Paul Judge -> /about", "Ontario, California facility opened 2013 -> /about", "33 facilities, 3,500+ employees, 4.7M+ sq ft -> /about, /", "Processes: Extrusion Blow Molding, Injection Stretch Blow Molding, Injection Blow Molding, Injection Molding, Tube Extrusion, Decoration -> /capabilities", "Industries served: Personal Care & Beauty, Healthcare & Nutraceuticals, Food, Beverage & Spirits, Home & Fabric Care -> /about", "Customers: Unilever, P&G, L''Oreal, Bath & Body Works, Diageo -> /about", "Vertix Recycling subsidiary produces PCR resin -> /capabilities", "GFSI FSSC 22000 V6 certification -> /capabilities", "Minority-certified supplier -> /about", "Speed-to-market: reduces lead times from weeks to days -> /", "Near-site manufacturing model -> /capabilities", "In-house design studio, 3D modeling, tool shops -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Axium Packaging is a leading manufacturer of packaging solutions for multinational consumer product companies", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "3,500+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Minority-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='axium-packaging-ca-plant' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Axon Circuit, Inc. is a printed circuit board manufacturer headquartered in Tampa, Florida. The company was founded in 1990 and has operated continuously in the Southeast United States for over three decades.

The firm produces rigid PCBs ranging from single-sided and double-sided boards to multilayer constructions up to 16 layers. Its capabilities include fine-line and surface-mount technology pitches, board thicknesses from 0.008 to 0.250 inches, carbon ink contacts, oversized multilayer panels, ball grid array patterns, blind and buried vias, peelable and water-soluble masks, plated slots and edges, epoxy via plug, and controlled impedance. Materials stocked encompass FR-4, high-temperature FR-4 equivalents, Rogers, Taconic, Arlon, polyimide, Teflon, and GETEK laminates. Surface finishes offered are solder mask over bare copper, hot air solder leveling, electroless nickel/gold (including bondable gold), electroless white tin, electroless silver, screenable silver and carbon, and heavy copper layers. The 25,000-square-foot facility employs more than 40 people and has produced over 100 million rigid PCBs, with annual revenue exceeding $5 million. The company owns its equipment and recently invested over $1 million in new fabrication and testing systems.

Axon Circuit serves customers in communications, instrumentation and controls, consumer electronics, medical devices, automotive, and military sectors. Its clientele is primarily business-to-business, built largely through referrals.

