UPDATE companies SET description='BIO El Paso–Juárez operates as a binational industry cluster organization headquartered in El Paso, Texas. Formed as a 501(c)(6) nonprofit under the Medical Center of the Americas Foundation, it was established to strengthen the medical device sector spanning the U.S.–Mexico border. A board led by Chair Julio Chiu and Vice Chair Mylena Walker governs the initiative, which formally links the Medical Center of the Americas Foundation with the Clúster Biomédico de Juárez.

The organization does not manufacture products. Instead, it convenes manufacturers, government agencies, academic institutions, and nonprofits to develop regional capabilities, map supply-chain competencies, and monitor cluster growth. Its programs create collaborative networks, promote the region’s biomedical ecosystem globally, and leverage the strategic El Paso–Juárez location to optimize cost, efficiency, and quality for member companies.

